    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green (the single `AcceptanceTest`, including the new `coreComposesSalutation`).\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `salutation` rule with low structural impact. `salutation` = `title + ' ' + lastName`, or just `lastName` when no title is given.\n\nFive files touched, no existing method bodies rewritten:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an optional `title` input field to `OwnerFields` and a read-only `salutation` field to `Owner` (drives the generated DTOs).\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `title` column field plus a small `getTitle`/`setTitle` pair (no existing method changed; MapStruct auto-maps `title` in both directions).\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one new `@Mapping` line deriving `salutation` via inline expression, mirroring how `displayName`/`contactPreference` are derived. Placed here (small class) rather than as a method on the large `Owner` entity to keep the surrounding-complexity cost low.\n4. **`db/hsqldb/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the `title` column to the `owners` table (test profile is `hsqldb`, `ddl-auto=none`).\n5. **`db/hsqldb/data.sql`** \u2014 appended a trailing `NULL` to the ten positional seed `INSERT`s so they still match the widened table.\n\nNo new function classes, no endpoint YAML changes \u2014 `title` flows in through the existing `BuildOwner \u2192 toOwner` mapping and is persisted like the other fields, so `GET /api/owners/{id}` reconstructs the salutation from the stored entity.",
